      "baseline_rule": "Before trusting delta narratives, verify the Previous/baseline car is stock: cross-check bars + hp + weight + top speed + 0-60 + latG against a car-database stock sheet (kudosprime/calculators.games). A livery icon on the card is NOT evidence of modification. New-column targets are absolute and never depend on this check.",
      "allocation_insight": "TWO DIFFERENT 800s: same car, same PI, different part allocation = measurably different cars. The compare pane's live diff QUANTIFIES allocation choices (e.g. race suspension + brakes vs one weight tier + engine trim: -0.29s 0-60 for the weight build). PI-identity is not build-identity — matching the PI number certifies nothing; matching every Car Stat row does.",
      "pane_blind_spots": "The compare pane CANNOT see: transmission tier/gear count, driveline, differential tier, tire width, track width (and brakes only indirectly via the braking bar). DOCTRINE REFINEMENT: 'certified replica' = all visible rows matched + PI exact — functionally certified, but blind-spot parts can differ underneath. Driving forensics covers some blind spots: HUD gear count (transmission), 0-60 convergence at equal weight (gearbox character), diff behavior on corner exit.",
      "video_forensics_note": "Short gameplay clips are a first-class instrument: frame extraction reads HUD speed/gear/skill-popups per instant. The skill system doubles as telemetry — DRIFT skills during a grip lap = rear slip detected; 'Great Speed' stamps entry speeds; wrecked-scenery skills timestamp off-track moments. 8-10s of video around one corner beats any verbal description.",
