      "peak_percent_proof": {
        "date": "2026-08-21",
        "method": "38 Friction-page frames transcribed (2 s steps) and cross-correlated against the Data Out capture over offsets -60..+60 s and hold windows 0/0.5/1/2/3 s for combined slip, slip ratio, slip angle.",
        "result": "Peak% == |TireCombinedSlip| x 100, INSTANTANEOUS (hold window 0 beat 0.5 s: median log-error 0.086 vs 0.232). Slip ratio/angle fit far worse. Offset -26.4 s (ShareX mtime lags recording end by ~26 s; align by content, not file time).",
        "examples": "on-screen 800/811 vs stream 803/812; 1,018/1,023 vs 1,019/1,002; 391/297/560/375 vs 390/309/560/426; 153/118/47/34 vs 158/121/59/30. Mismatches only where slip changes fast between 2 s samples.",
        "consequence": "The whole friction-diagnosis framework (first red ring, axle x phase matrix, Peak% bands) is now computable from the stream at 139 Hz with no HUD. Red ring == |CombinedSlip| > 1.0."
      },
      "telemetry_lab": "v0 BUILT 2026-08-21: dashboard tab Telemetry Lab with two views over session JSON (scripts/telemetry/analyze_session.py): LAB RUN = tiles, per-second session strip with car lanes, phase-segmented corner cards (first red ring, USI, matrix cell + fix), launch slip traces, braking wheel-speed-deficit lock table, per-car gear ladder + dyno, yaw-decay + bottoming counts, HUD-clip slots; DECODE BENCH = donor/replica selectors, maneuver rail, overlays (gear ladder, dyno, launch slip, braking deficits), match ledger with traffic lights + turn-next doctrine per slider group. Demo data = different cars from the first capture.",
      "live_mode": "BUILT 2026-08-21: scripts/telemetry/fh6_live_daemon.py (UDP -> CSV + Server-Sent Events on http://localhost:8765; --replay <csv> [--speed N] replays any recording through the same pipeline; auto-runs analyze_session.py when driving stops >5 s and serves /session.json). Dashboard Telemetry Lab -> Live: friction circles (Peak% = |combined slip| x 100, needle = slip vector, ring red >1.0), live tiles, growing strip, corner log, one-click open of the auto-analyzed session in Lab Run. Verified at 237 pkt/s replay.",
      "live_advisor": "BUILT 2026-08-21: per-config probe coverage (12 probes with required counts, confidence, next-drive hints) + rule-based ranked advice; daemon re-analyzes every ~20 s of driving; Live + Lab Run render confidence bars and suggestions per car.",
      "surface_fields": "No surface-type enum in the stream. Proxies: SurfaceRumble (per wheel, FFB magnitude) — on the tarmac run 2026-08-21 it read exactly 0 for 95% of frames and a discrete 0.6 otherwise (3,274 frames), suggesting a per-material constant; WheelOnRumbleStrip 0/1 (never seen yet); WheelInPuddle (never nonzero yet). TODO: calibration drive over grass/gravel/dirt/sand/rumble strips/water to map SurfaceRumble levels -> surface, then add a surface lane to the strip and dirt-specific probes (grip-slide spectrum)."
